      // Restore the saved meta preference. The ThemeService adopts its
      // durable built-in preference ("light"/"dark"/"system") from the Host
      // settings scope and republishes it each time that document is
      // re-read — on boot, and again after every profile recomposition
      // (switching provider/model rewrites the profile and triggers one).
      //
      // `adopt()` only publishes `theme/change`; it never calls setTheme.
      // The user clicking a built-in appearance in Settings → General does
      // call setTheme. That asymmetry is the only reliable signal separating
      // a Host echo from a deliberate choice, because the two carry identical
      // payloads. It also survives past page load, which the old fixed
      // five-second boot window did not — a model switch happens whenever,
      // and outside that window the pack simply lost the preference.
